Title: Of One Blood
Order: 24
Production Code: 1x24

EXT. OPEN COUNTRY NEAR LIVINGSTON HALL - NIGHT

AMB: wind over empty fields

[[Aubrey Livingston]] has walked since dawn, unable to stop asking himself the same question.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
(to himself)
I wonder if she lives.

Two figures cross his path, hand in hand — [[Dianthe Lusk]], in the white she died in; then, on his way home, [[Molly Vance]], her face turned accusingly toward him. Neither speaks. Both vanish.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON (CONT'D)
(shaken, almost hopeful)
'Twas she. In full life. God of heaven, she lives—

INT. LIVINGSTON HALL - DIANTHE'S ROOM - CONTINUOUS

He climbs the stairs and opens the door on the truth: Dianthe laid out in white, [[Reuel Briggs]] kneeling at her side. [[Charlie Vance]], [[Ai]], and [[Ababdis]] rise to meet him.

CHARLIE VANCE
Welcome, murderer.

Legal charges follow, funded lawyers follow, and Aubrey's wealth buys him out of every one of them. But one visit is never entered into any court record.

INT. LIVINGSTON HALL - AUBREY'S STUDY - NIGHT (LATER)

AMB: a single lamp

[[Ai]], [[Ababdis]], [[Hannah]], and [[Reuel Briggs]] stand silently around Aubrey's chair.

AI
Peace, O son of Osiris, to thy parting hour.

Ai circles him, chanting low, then fixes him with a stare Aubrey cannot break. Aubrey's eyes close, unwilling, into trance.

AI (CONT'D)
(bent to his ear, unheard by the others)

Ai straightens, makes a final pass over Aubrey's face, and the group leaves as quietly as they came.

CHARLIE VANCE
(in the carriage after)
Is justice done?

AI
Justice will be done.

EXT. CHARLES RIVER - DAY (DAYS LATER)

AMB: the river, indifferent

Aubrey Livingston's body is found floating at the exact bend where Molly Vance once floated — his own executioner, exactly as Telassar's ancient law required of any member of the royal line found guilty of murder.

INT. TELASSAR - THRONE HALL - DAY (LATER)

MUSIC: IN - ceremonial, warm

[[Reuel Briggs]] returns to Telassar for good, [[Hannah]] with him, and rules beside [[Queen Candace]] — teaching his people what he learned of the modern world, and watching, uneasily, as that same world presses closer every year to the mysterious forests hiding his people from it.

REUEL BRIGGS
(quiet, to himself)
Of one blood, all of it. I only wish it hadn't taken so much dying to prove it.

MUSIC: OUT
